WEBVTT

00:00:03.995 --> 00:00:09.074
Sometimes you want nothing on screen but your text. That's what focus mode is for.

00:00:09.374 --> 00:00:16.010
Press Ctrl+Shift+Enter, or choose Focus Mode from the menu. The sidebar and toolbars step aside.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:23.287
As you type, the line you're writing stays in the middle of the screen, like on a typewriter. Your eyes don't have to wander.

00:00:29.544 --> 00:00:33.769
Everything except the paragraph you're working on fades into the background.

00:00:34.548 --> 00:00:40.160
The formatting bar stays at hand. Move the pointer to the top edge, and the header bar comes back.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:50.702
In the preferences, focus mode can have its own font, size and theme, like a dark one just for writing. You can also switch off typewriter scrolling and dimming there.

00:00:53.828 --> 00:00:57.947
Press Escape to leave focus mode. Everything is back where it was.

00:00:58.247 --> 00:00:59.934
Just you and your text.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.566
Typecase. Free software, made for GNOME.

00:01:03.866 --> 00:01:06.448
With love, by kleinod.studio.
